# What never belongs in the image.
#
# The first entry is the important one: `.env` holds the OpenSky client secret
# and the aisstream key, and `COPY app ./app` would not pick it up today - but
# a future `COPY . .` would, and a secret baked into an image layer is a secret
# published to everyone who can pull it. Excluding it here means that change
# cannot quietly leak them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The virtualenv is Windows-built and would be wrong in a Linux image even if
# it were small, which at several hundred megabytes it is not.
.venv/
venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests and their fixtures are not needed to serve traffic. They run in CI and
# on a developer's machine, where the network is allowed to be absent.
tests/

# Whatever the accounts database happens to hold locally. The container makes
# its own at `/srv/data`.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3
data/

.git/
.gitignore
*.md
